   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing region by region. Stereochemistry is only partly taken from the drawing.\n\n**Left: tri-antennary GalNAc cluster.**\n- Each of the three arms is: quaternary C\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)NH\u2013(CH2)3\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013(CH2)4\u2013O\u2013\u03b2-GalNAc.\n- The sugar stereochemistry was written as \u03b2-D-GalNAc (N-acetylgalactosamine), converted from the known N-acetylgalactosamine SMILES.\n\n**Centre: PEG linker.**\n- The quaternary carbon carries an NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2 group, then nine ether oxygens separated by eight CH2CH2 units.\n- The linker ends in CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)NH, which attaches to the lysine side-chain nitrogen.\n\n**Right: macrocyclic peptide.** Reading around the ring from the thioether, the sequence is:\n\n1. S\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013 (chloroacetyl-derived) on the N-terminal Phe\n2. Phe\n3. Arg\n4. N-Me-Phe\n5. Ser\n6. Lys (side chain carries the PEG)\n7. Asn\n8. Tyr\n9. N-Me-Gly (sarcosine)\n10. Arg\n11. Asp\n12. Tic (tetrahydroisoquinoline-3-carboxylic acid)\n13. Asn\n14. N-Me-Phe\n15. Cys (its sulfur closes the thioether ring)\n16. Gly-NH2 as the C-terminus\n\nI assigned L configuration to all the standard residues by default. I did not verify each wedge against the drawing, so some residues (for example the N-terminal Phe) may actually be D.\n\nSMILES: S1CC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)CCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCCC(=O)NC(COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]3O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]3NC(C)=O)(COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]3O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]3NC(C)=O)COCCC(=O)NCCCNC(=O)CCCCO[C@@H]3O[C@H](CO)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]3NC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)O)C(=O)N2Cc3ccccc3C[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS1)C(=O)NCC(N)=O"
